openstack-placement — OpenStack Placement 16.0.0 (2026.2 Hibiscus)
====================================================================

This package installs the Placement resource-tracking service. It
installs software ONLY: nothing is enabled, started, migrated or
credentialed at install time.

What it ships
-------------

  /usr/bin/placement-manage        administrative CLI (db sync, ...)
  /usr/bin/placement-status        status CLI
  placement.wsgi.api:application   the supported WSGI application
  placement/db/sqlalchemy/alembic/ database migration scripts
  /usr/share/placement/config-generator.conf   config generator input
  /etc/init.d/placement            OpenRC service (gunicorn)
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/placement.service   systemd service (gunicorn)
  /etc/conf.d/placement            WSGI container runtime settings

Operator steps (NOT performed by this package)
----------------------------------------------

1. Render and edit the configuration (no sample placement.conf ships
   upstream; generate from the shipped generator input):

     oslo-config-generator \
       --config-file /usr/share/placement/config-generator.conf \
       --output-file /etc/placement/placement.conf
     # edit /etc/placement/placement.conf (database, keystone auth, ...).
     # No database driver is installed by this package: add
     # python-pymysql for MariaDB, or use sqlite for trials.

2. Initialise the database:

     placement-manage db_sync

3. Register the service and endpoints in Keystone (operator-chosen).

4. Enable and start the service explicitly:

     rc-update add placement default && rc-service placement start
     # or
     systemctl enable --now placement

Placement is served by gunicorn; nginx/haproxy fronting it for TLS is
an optional, operator-configured choice.

Independence
------------

Placement depends on the native python closure, gunicorn and the
keystone middleware libraries. It does not depend on Nova, Neutron,
Cinder, Glance or QEMU, and it can be installed on its own.
